-- zip: pair up corresponding elements of two lists.
-- Written as an arrow graph over list primitives.
-- Contract: inferred from the loop body.
--
-- Graph structure:
--   zip = rec { first(arr("list.head")) >>> (first(arr("list.tail")) >>> arr("list.cons")) }
--
-- The loop processes elements one at a time:
--   - take the head of both lists (first component)
--   - take the tail of both lists (advance both)
--   - cons the pair onto the output
--   - repeat until either list is exhausted

zip = rec { first(arr("list.head")) >>> (first(arr("list.tail")) >>> arr("list.cons")) }
